<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Rodez</h1><p class="st-meta">1112 CE – 1589 CE (approx.) · capital Rodez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The county of the Rouergue around Rodez, held by the Millau and Armagnac families, which shared its hilltop city with a powerful bishop.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The county of Rouergue had belonged to the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a>. In 1112 the viscount of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millau">Millau</a>, Richard, acquired the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a>, founding a local line that ruled the comital part of the city, the Bourg, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> governed the Cité around the cathedral.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rouergue was a land of uplands, sheep and pilgrim routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Compostela</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conques">Conques</a> nearby. Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-count-of-rodez">Henry II of Rodez</a> was a patron of troubadours in the late 13th century. In 1302 his daughter Cécile brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-vi-of-armagnac">Bernard VI of Armagnac</a>, and the county became one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-armagnac">Armagnacs</a>' chief holdings.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-armagnac">Armagnac</a> line ended, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a> passed to the Alençon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-albret">Albret</a> families and so to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry of Navarre</a>. When he became Henry IV in 1589, the county joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>; his personal lands were formally united with the crown in 1607.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-rodez.jpg" alt="County of Rodez" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: Ayack · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_comtes_de_Rodez.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1112 CE – 1589 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rodez</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry II of Rodez, Bernard VI of Armagnac</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Occitan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rouergue</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1350&amp;focus=county-of-rodez" aria-label="County of Rodez on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4742 609 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Rodez lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5062 865L5035 888M5062 865L5014 887M5062 865L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5035 888h0M5014 887h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5062 865h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5062 865h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rodez. <a href="/atlas?year=1350&amp;focus=county-of-rodez">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
